jeka.properties<pre><code># Make 'base:' optional on the command line (e.g. 'jeka pack')
jeka.kbean.default=base

# Needed for publishing
@base.moduleId=org.example:my-app
@base.gitVersioning.enable=true

# FAT by default
@base.jarType=REGULAR

# Used by runMain and runJar
@base.jvmOptions=-Xmx256m
@base.programArgs=arg1 arg2
</code></pre> <p>There is no <code>version</code> property. Use <code>@base.gitVersioning.enable=true</code> as above, or <code>@maven.pub.version</code> for publishing.  See Maven KBean.</p>

jeka.properties<pre><code># Use absolute paths instead of the JEKA_USER_HOME variable
@eclipse.useVarPath=false

# Use a specific JRE
@eclipse.jreContainer=org.eclipse.jdt.launching.JRE_CONTAINER/org.eclipse.jdt.internal.debug.ui.launcher.StandardVMType/JavaSE-21
</code></pre>

Configuration in a Build.java class<pre><code>@JkPostInit
private void postInit(IntellijKBean intellijKBean) {
    intellijKBean
            .replaceLibByModule("dev.jeka.jeka-core.jar", "core")
            .setModuleAttributes("core", JkIntellijIml.Scope.COMPILE, null);
}
</code></pre>
